Your repository is not a backup of the CMS. It is the content store.

Structured fields use stable JSON. Long-form text uses Markdoc. Images sit beside the entry that uses them. The same input always produces the same file order, so reviews show the change that matters.

## One publish, one commit

Saves accumulate as drafts, and all editors see them. On the Publish page, the editor chooses which changes to publish. Publish writes the chosen changes — entries, sidecar files, and media together — as one Git commit. In the self-hosted editor, the editor is the author of the commit and Mica is the committer, and Mica pushes it over HTTPS to any Git host. The local editor commits in your checkout with your own Git identity.

The self-hosted editor keeps its own clone and syncs it on its own. It fetches the branch and fast-forwards. It never merges.
